issue.body:
I noticed in my template a `range` stopped working. I tried to simplify to get to the key issue and found that if I had this in a template
```
{{- $CCC := 1 | int }}
{{- $CCC = add1 $CCC }}
```

i would get the error
```
Error: render error in "voltha/templates/rw-core.yaml": template: voltha/templates/rw-core.yaml:43:26: executing "voltha/templates/rw-core.yaml" at <$CCC>: wrong type for value; expected int; got int64
```

I think there is a math/type problem at the core of my range problem. my original range statement was a simple iterate 

{{ range $i, $e := until (int .Values.count) }}

